\begin_layout Subsection
BiocFrame:
 A Flexible DataFrame
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
BiocFrame
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "noauthor_biocpybiocframe_2025"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 class implements the semantics of Bioconductor's 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
DFrame
\end_layout

\end_inset

 (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
DataFrame
\end_layout

\end_inset

) class from 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
S4Vectors
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "h_pages_s4vectors_2017"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 and serves as the primary metadata container across the BiocPy ecosystem.
 While pandas 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
DataFrame
\end_layout

\end_inset

s are standard in Python data analysis,
 they enforce columnar type homogeneity backed by NumPy or Arrow arrays.
 In genomic workflows,
 this can lead to unwanted type coercion (such as casting integers to floats when missing values are introduced) and makes it difficult to store complex domain objects as columns.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In contrast,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
BiocFrame
\end_layout

\end_inset

 makes minimal assumptions about its columns:
 any object that defines a length (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
__len__
\end_layout

\end_inset

) equal to the number of rows and supports slicing (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
__getitem__
\end_layout

\end_inset

) can be stored as a column.
 This protocol-based design preserves original data types and allows arbitrarily nested or specialized columns such as another 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
BiocFrame
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 a 2D NumPy array,
 a 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
GenomicRanges
\end_layout

\end_inset

 object,
 or a compressed list of intervals,
 to be sliced and combined alongside standard 1D vectors.
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
BiocFrame
\end_layout

\end_inset

 also supports Bioconductor's metadata members,
 including 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
column_data
\end_layout

\end_inset

 (a 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
BiocFrame
\end_layout

\end_inset

 describing the columns) and 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
metadata
\end_layout

\end_inset

 (an arbitrary dictionary describing the table).
 When users need general tabular operations or plotting utilities,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
BiocFrame
\end_layout

\end_inset

 provides direct conversion methods (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
to_pandas()
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
from_pandas()
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
to_polars()
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
from_polars()
\end_layout

\end_inset

) to interoperate with pandas and Polars
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "noauthor_pola-rspolars_2025"
literal "false"

\end_inset

,
 though converting to flat tabular formats may omit nested metadata or specialized column types.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
GenomicRanges and Interval Representations
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Interval arithmetic on genomic coordinates is a core requirement of many sequencing workflows.
 In Bioconductor,
 genomic intervals are represented using the 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
IRanges
\end_layout

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
GenomicRanges
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "lawrence_software_2013"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 packages.
 In Python,
 interval operations have typically been performed by wrapping command-line utilities such as bedtools
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "quinlan_bedtools_2010"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 or using tabular libraries such as PyRanges
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "stovner_pyranges_2020"
literal "false"

\end_inset

.
 BiocPy provides native,
 in-memory implementations of 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
IRanges
\end_layout

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
GenomicRanges
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "noauthor_biocpygenomicranges_2025"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 that follow Bioconductor's coordinate and strand semantics.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Unlike a generic table with chromosome,
 start,
 and end columns,
 a 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
GenomicRanges
\end_layout

\end_inset

 object couples integer intervals (via an 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
IRanges
\end_layout

\end_inset

 instance storing start positions and widths) with sequence names (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
seqnames
\end_layout

\end_inset

),
 strand orientation (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
+
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
-
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 or 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
*
\end_layout

\end_inset

),
 feature-level metadata (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
mcols
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 stored as a 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
BiocFrame
\end_layout

\end_inset

),
 and reference genome metadata (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
SeqInfo
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 tracking chromosome lengths and circularity).
 This structure enforces coordinate validity and strand-aware arithmetic across operations including overlap detection (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
find_overlaps()
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
count_overlaps()
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
subset_by_overlaps()
\end_layout

\end_inset

),
 proximity queries (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
nearest()
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
precede()
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
follow()
\end_layout

\end_inset

),
 intra-range transformations (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
shift()
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
resize()
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
flank()
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
promoters()
\end_layout

\end_inset

),
 and inter-range set operations (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
reduce()
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
gaps()
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
disjoin()
\end_layout

\end_inset

).
 For example,
 calling 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
promoters()
\end_layout

\end_inset

 on gene annotations automatically accounts for strand direction when computing upstream and downstream coordinates relative to transcription start sites.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To represent grouped genomic intervals such as exons grouped by transcript or peaks grouped by sample,
 BiocPy also implements 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
CompressedGenomicRangesList
\end_layout

\end_inset

 (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
GenomicRangesList
\end_layout

\end_inset

).
 Built on the 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
CompressedList
\end_layout

\end_inset

 abstraction,
 all constituent ranges are stored in a single contiguous 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
GenomicRanges
\end_layout

\end_inset

 object alongside an integer partitioning vector.
 This avoids the memory and iteration overhead of instantiating thousands of separate Python objects while allowing vectorized operations across groups.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To support interval queries in Python,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
iranges
\end_layout

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
genomicranges
\end_layout

\end_inset

 delegate overlap and proximity searches to a C++ implementation of the nested containment list data structure
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "alekseyenko_nested_2007"
literal "false"

\end_inset

 (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
nclist-cpp
\end_layout

\end_inset

),
 with built-in multi-threading support (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
num_threads
\end_layout

\end_inset

).
 Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
